# Every Engine v2 program on a machine shared with today's system (Engine v2 O17, #2810): the worlds (worldd@), the
# gateways, the directory and the origin. Memory is capped at 12 GB: the largest world's own cap (Eden, 8 GB in
# world-limits.json; it idles at about 1.9 GB) plus 4 GB for the gateways (512 MB each at most), the directory
# (256 MB), the origin (1 GB for all its processes) and the small worlds (2 GB each at most, a few hundred MB settled). On the production host
# (30.6 GiB) that leaves 18.6 GiB for today's system (its production cap is 9 GB, docs/operations.md) and the host.
# The processor and the disk are shared, never capped: at weight 20 against the default 100 the new system gets a
# fifth of what today's gets when both are busy, and all of it when today's is idle, so neither system's world time is
# throttled. A world's own limit (worldd@'s 2 GB, or its limits.conf from world-limits.json) holds inside.
[Unit]
Description=Souls Engine v2 programs

[Slice]
MemoryMax=12G
MemorySwapMax=0
CPUWeight=20
IOWeight=20
TasksMax=4096
